  "checks": [
    "Default empty compiled authority falls through to unchanged pinned V1 baseline; all four historical artifact checks reproduce exact bytes.",
    "Adopted V2 rails reconstruct exact authored candidate, require complete factual and independently identified quality judgments, then require exact saved proposal, current native runtime/source audit and final acceptance by the corresponding independent initial reviewers.",
    "Artifact/source pins alone cannot grant authority: missing documents, rejected raw facts, shared reviewer identity, held final reviews and rehashed stale audit bindings refuse.",
    "Source-chain schema enforces sequential versions, exact predecessor digests, unique paths/digests and bounded length; sources and archived descriptors are reread and hashed. A future unadopted candidate does not gain approval from a source digest alone.",
    "Only the two exact metadata paths are excluded from the runtime manifest. The Go pin must equal its fixed metadata-only template; extra functions, declarations, imports or even comment drift refuse. All earlier runtime inputs and installed.go remain audited.",
    "Protected authority reads require bounded regular files, non-symlinked parents, matching opened-FD identity and rechecked path identities; path escapes, symlinked parents, directories and oversized documents refuse.",
    "Adoption and draft generation recheck all seven descriptors, runtime/source inventories and metadata before success. Installation readsets include both excluded metadata files, registered source chains, archives and authority documents; guarded installation retains existing compare-and-swap and rollback checks.",
    "Draft outputs explicitly protect both metadata paths and every runtimePaths input, as well as supplied source/review inputs and fixture/source directories."
  ],
